 "titulo": {
  "estudio": "¿Te has enterado?",
  "alumno": "Have you heard?"
 },
 "intro": "The small words that make a conversation sound native: opening, reacting, digressing, interrupting and winding up.",
 "palabras": [
  {
   "palabra": "enterarse de",
   "significado": "to find out, to hear about",
   "pron": "en-te-RAR-se de",
   "ipa": "",
   "cat": "verb",
   "genero": "",
   "plural": "",
   "definida": "",
   "consejo": "It is pronominal and takes «de»: «me enteré de la noticia». The typical question is «¿te has enterado?».",
   "nota": "",
   "oculta": false
  },
  {
   "palabra": "no me digas",
   "significado": "you don't say!",
   "pron": "no me DI-gas",
   "ipa": "",
   "cat": "set expression",
   "genero": "",
   "plural": "",
   "definida": "",
   "consejo": "It is not an order: it is a reaction of surprise. You say it when someone tells you something surprising.",
   "nota": "",
   "oculta": false
  },
  {
   "palabra": "anda",
   "significado": "well!, wow!",
   "pron": "AN-da",
   "ipa": "",
   "cat": "interjection",
   "genero": "",
   "plural": "",
   "definida": "",
   "consejo": "It comes from «andar», but here it only shows surprise. It also works to urge: «¡anda, cuenta!».",
   "nota": "",
   "oculta": false
  },
  {
   "palabra": "alucinante",
   "significado": "amazing, incredible",
   "pron": "a-lu-thi-NAN-te",
   "ipa": "",
   "cat": "adjective",
   "genero": "",
   "plural": "",
   "definida": "",
   "consejo": "It is colloquial. It ends in -ante and does not change with gender: «un plan alucinante», «una idea alucinante».",
   "nota": "",
   "oculta": false
  },
  {
   "palabra": "me lo imagino",
   "significado": "I can imagine",
   "pron": "me lo i-ma-HI-no",
   "ipa": "",
   "cat": "set expression",
   "genero": "",
   "plural": "",
   "definida": "",
   "consejo": "It is pronominal: «me lo imagino». It is used to say «I understand» or «I believe it».",
   "nota": "",
   "oculta": false
  },
  {
   "palabra": "pues verás",
   "significado": "well, you see",
   "pron": "pwes be-RAS",
   "ipa": "",
   "cat": "set expression",
   "genero": "",
   "plural": "",
   "definida": "",
   "consejo": "It is said before telling something. «Verás» is the future of «ver» and has an accent.",
   "nota": "",
   "oculta": false
  },
  {
   "palabra": "total que",
   "significado": "so, in the end",
   "pron": "to-TAL ke",
   "ipa": "",
   "cat": "set expression",
   "genero": "",
   "plural": "",
   "definida": "",
   "consejo": "It jumps to the end of a story: «total, que no fuimos». A comma follows «total».",
   "nota": "",
   "oculta": false
  },
  {
   "palabra": "en fin",
   "significado": "anyway, in short",
   "pron": "en fin",
   "ipa": "",
   "cat": "set expression",
   "genero": "",
   "plural": "",
   "definida": "",
   "consejo": "It is used when finishing an explanation or when something cannot be helped. It goes between commas.",
   "nota": "",
   "oculta": false
  },
  {
   "palabra": "cambiando de tema",
   "significado": "changing the subject",
   "pron": "kam-BYAN-do de TE-ma",
   "ipa": "",
   "cat": "set expression",
   "genero": "",
   "plural": "",
   "definida": "",
   "consejo": "It is a gerund that opens another matter. Another form is «cambiemos de tema».",
   "nota": "",
   "oculta": false
  },
  {
   "palabra": "hablando de",
   "significado": "speaking of",
   "pron": "a-BLAN-do de",
   "ipa": "",
   "cat": "set expression",
   "genero": "",
   "plural": "",
   "definida": "",
   "consejo": "The new topic follows: «hablando de viajes, …». It is a fixed gerund.",
   "nota": "",
   "oculta": false
  },
  {
   "palabra": "perdona que te interrumpa",
   "significado": "sorry to interrupt",
   "pron": "per-DO-na ke te in-te-RRUM-pa",
   "ipa": "",
   "cat": "set expression",
   "genero": "",
   "plural": "",
   "definida": "",
   "consejo": "After «perdona que» comes the subjunctive: «interrumpa», not «interrumpo». With «usted»: «perdone que le interrumpa».",
   "nota": "",
   "oculta": false
  },
  {
   "palabra": "antes de que se me olvide",
   "significado": "before I forget",
   "pron": "AN-tes de ke se me ol-BI-de",
   "ipa": "",
   "cat": "set expression",
   "genero": "",
   "plural": "",
   "definida": "",
   "consejo": "After «antes de que» the subjunctive always goes: «olvide». «Se me olvida» is forgetting without meaning to.",
   "nota": "",
   "oculta": false
  },
  {
   "palabra": "como decía",
   "significado": "as I was saying",
   "pron": "KO-mo de-THI-a",
   "ipa": "",
   "cat": "set expression",
   "genero": "",
   "plural": "",
   "definida": "",
   "consejo": "It serves to pick up an idea after an interruption. «Decía» is the imperfect of «decir».",
   "nota": "",
   "oculta": false
  },
  {
   "palabra": "adelante",
   "significado": "go ahead",
   "pron": "a-de-LAN-te",
   "ipa": "",
   "cat": "adverb",
   "genero": "",
   "plural": "",
   "definida": "",
   "consejo": "It is said to give way or the floor. It is written as one word: «adelante».",
   "nota": "",
   "oculta": false
  },
  {
   "palabra": "perfectamente",
   "significado": "perfectly",
   "pron": "per-fek-ta-MEN-te",
   "ipa": "",
   "cat": "adverb",
   "genero": "",
   "plural": "",
   "definida": "",
   "consejo": "Adverb from «perfecta». The -mente ending turns an adjective into an adverb.",
   "nota": "",
   "oculta": false
  },
  {
   "palabra": "olvide",
   "significado": "forget (olvidar), subjunctive",
   "pron": "ol-BI-de",
   "ipa": "",
   "cat": "verb",
   "genero": "",
   "plural": "",
   "definida": "",
   "consejo": "After «que» with a wish, use the subjunctive: «que olvide».",
   "nota": "",
   "oculta": false
  },
  {
   "palabra": "viajes",
   "significado": "trips, travels",
   "pron": "BYA-jes",
   "ipa": "",
   "cat": "noun",
   "genero": "m",
   "plural": "",
   "definida": "",
   "consejo": "Plural of «viaje». The j sounds like h.",
   "nota": "",
   "oculta": false
  },
  {
   "palabra": "preguntarte",
   "significado": "to ask you (preguntar)",
   "pron": "pre-gun-TAR-te",
   "ipa": "",
   "cat": "verb",
   "genero": "",
   "plural": "",
   "definida": "",
   "consejo": "«te» joins the infinitive. «quiero preguntarte» means I want to ask you.",
   "nota": "",
   "oculta": false
  },
  {
   "palabra": "llovizna",
   "significado": "drizzle",
   "pron": "yo-BIZ-na",
   "ipa": "",
   "cat": "noun",
   "genero": "f",
   "plural": "",
   "definida": "",
   "consejo": "A very light rain. The ll sounds like y.",
   "nota": "",
   "oculta": false
  },
  {
   "palabra": "inclina",
   "significado": "leans (inclinarse)",
   "pron": "in-KLI-na",
   "ipa": "",
   "cat": "verb",
   "genero": "",
   "plural": "",
   "definida": "",
   "consejo": "«inclinarse» means to bend or lean forward.",
   "nota": "",
   "oculta": false
  },
  {
   "palabra": "contara",
   "significado": "would tell (contar), subjunctive",
   "pron": "kon-TA-ra",
   "ipa": "",
   "cat": "verb",
   "genero": "",
   "plural": "",
   "definida": "",
   "consejo": "«como si» is followed by the subjunctive: «como si contara».",
   "nota": "",
   "oculta": false
  },
  {
   "palabra": "secreto",
   "significado": "secret",
   "pron": "se-KRE-to",
   "ipa": "",
   "cat": "noun",
   "genero": "m",
   "plural": "",
   "definida": "",
   "consejo": "Something kept hidden. The c before e sounds like «k».",
   "nota": "",
   "oculta": false
  },
  {
   "palabra": "cucharillas",
   "significado": "teaspoons",
   "pron": "ku-cha-RI-llas",
   "ipa": "",
   "cat": "noun",
   "genero": "f",
   "plural": "",
   "definida": "",
   "consejo": "Small spoons. From «cuchara», with the diminutive «-illa».",
   "nota": "",
   "oculta": false
  },
  {
